or, precise_od</code></td></tr><tr><td>Solar limb-darkened SRP shadow (opt-in)</td><td>SRP lit fraction as the un-occulted fraction of the limb-darkened solar flux (Eddington-approximation law I(mu)/I(1) = 2/5 + 3/5 mu, Gauss-Legendre quadrature) over a spherical or WGS-84 Earth (srp_shadow::limb_darkened_shadow, the ShadowModel variant OblateEarthLimbDarkened)</td><td>MODELLED</td><td>None external: Orekit 12.2 has no limb-darkened lighting ratio. Checked against closed forms of the same law only</td><td><code>srp_shadow</code></td></tr><tr><td>NRLMSISE-00 thermospheric density</td><td>A port of the NRLMSISE-00 empirical thermosphere (gtd7 and gtd7d: species densities, total mass density with anomalous oxygen, temperatures; the 24 switches; daily-Ap and 3-hourly ap-array modes) from the public-domain C version of the NRL Fortran</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>pymsis 0.13.0 (MIT) version=0, which runs the NRL Fortran GTD7D in single precision, and the NRLMSISE-00 C port (release 20190709, public domain) compiled as a separate program, plus the C distribution's 17 published test outputs. Bars pre-registered in xval/nrlmsise00-pymsis/PREREGISTRATION.md (a6504ec9) before the port existed; all met (RESULTS.md). Validates the port, not the model's accuracy against measured density</td><td><code>nrlmsise00</code></td></tr><tr><td>NRLMSISE-00 drag-density tier (opt-in)</td><td>forces::DensityModel (Exponential default, Nrlmsise00 { f107a, f107, ap }) and propagator::ForceModel::drag_density: quadratic drag against the co-rotating atmosphere with the NRLMSISE-00 density at the WGS-84 geodetic point (Earth rotation angle with UT1 = TT, local solar time UT + lon/15), constant space weather per model; default off and bit-identical</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>Orekit 12.2 (Apache-2.0) NumericalPropagator/DormandPrince853 with DragForce over Orekit's own NRLMSISE00 implementation, run as a separate program with the same Earth-rotation-angle frame, WGS-84 shape, local-solar-time conventi