on correction (rotate each node by ω⊕·(t_node−t) into the query instant's Earth-fixed frame before the polynomial fit)</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>RTKLIB peph2pos() compiled from C source (preceph.c; T. Takasu, BSD-2-Clause) — the de-facto IGS reference, an independent implementation; kshana's interpolator (now carrying the same Earth-rotation node correction) matched to ~15 nm on a real SP3 product, down from ~5.5 cm before the correction</td><td><code>sp3 (Sp3Interpolator::position_ecef)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Navigation-message encoders beyond GPS LNAV (GPS CNAV, Galileo I/NAV and F/NAV)</td><td>GPS CNAV message types 10/11/30, Galileo I/NAV word types 1-5 in nominal even/odd pages and Galileo F/NAV page types 1-4: ICD field packing and quantisation, CRC-24Q, rate-1/2 K=7 convolutional coding (G2 inverted for Galileo), block interleaving and sync patterns, with matching test decoders</td><td>MODELLED</td><td>Internal round trip and ICD known answers; no third-party decoder has been run (the RTKLIB/GNSS-SDR harness reading KSHANA_NAVMSG_ORACLE_JSON is data-gated). MODELLED</td><td><code>gnss_navmsg (gps_cnav, gal_inav, gal_fnav, fec)</code></td></tr><tr><td>IONEX global ionosphere map reader and interpolation on a real CODE GIM</td><td>IONEX 1.0 reader (header, fixed-column I5 values, TEC and RMS maps, absolute epochs, missing values) with bilinear spatial interpolation, the format's nearest / consecutive / rotated-map time interpolation (eqs. 1-3) and thin-shell slant TEC</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>The CODE GIM's printed values (exact at every node; the map is fetched at test time, not vendored, its licence being unconfirmed) and an independent Python stdlib re-implementation of the IONEX 1.0 interpolation formulas committed with the fixture (bars pre-registered 79beaab, 1e-9 TECU). Third-party check (B6, pre-registered, first run): RTKLIB v2.4.2-p13 iontec (BSD-2-Clause, run as a separate tool) at 6885 query points agrees with IonexFile::vtec_at to 3.6e-13 TECU in