M2008 truncated at degree 70, gravity_anomaly_sa, WGS84, tide-free, zero-degree term, h = 0. The service output carries no explicit licence, so the grids are fetched at test time with a pinned SHA-256 (tools/fetch_icgem_grid.sh) and only ten values are cited with attribution</td><td><code>gravity_sh, altpnt::maps, gravimeter</code></td></tr><tr><td>SRTM digital-elevation reader on real terrain</td><td>Hand-rolled SRTM .hgt parser (16-bit big-endian, north-row-first, void-aware) + bilinear sampler reading a real public-domain DEM tile and resolving a documented survey benchmark</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>NASA/USGS SRTM v3 (1-arc-second) N36W117 tile — US-Government PUBLIC-DOMAIN elevation data from the AWS elevation-tiles-prod open mirror, decimated to 6-arc-second and committed under tests/fixtures/terrain/ (see NOTICE.md), plus full-resolution crops of N36W117 and N36W119 cross-checked node-for-node against GDAL's independent SRTMHGT reader and the Mount Whitney (4421 m) and Badwater (−86 m) survey benchmarks. The documented Badwater Basin benchmark (−86 m, lowest in North America) anchors the geo-referenced read. The terrain-matching/TERCOM nav-fix that consumes the DEM stays Modelled (separate Alternative/complementary PNT row)</td><td><code>altpnt::terrain</code></td></tr><tr><td>Reproducibility &amp; software assurance</td><td>Deterministic, scenario-hashed, SBOM + cross-platform golden gates</td><td>MODELLED</td><td>SBOM conformance to the official CycloneDX 1.5 JSON Schema (+ valid SPDX identifiers) — an external published standard, zero validation errors over the full dependency graph; the FoM-determinism / byte-reproducibility part remains a pinned self-consistency check, so the row stays MODELLED</td><td><code>report, scenario; CI (golden/determinism/SBOM)</code></td></tr><tr><td>AI/ML RF-impairment detection evaluation (13494)</td><td>Labelled synthetic impairment corpus + detector-agnostic ROC/AUC/confusion/Pfa-Pmd harness; leakage guard, stratified split