c44b3) before any comparison: Orekit parses every Kshana-written message (14 AEM KVN, 11 AEM XML, 4 APM KVN, 4 APM XML) and every value is inside its bar (quaternions 1e-14, angles 1e-9 deg; worst 0.054 of a bar); Kshana parses the 31 messages Orekit writes from the same inputs inside every bar; the rotation of each of 135 quaternion, Euler and spin records equals AemSegment.getAngularCoordinates within 1e-12 (worst 0.0071 of the bar). All 15 Kshana XML messages validate against the NDM/XML 4.0.0 schema (data-gated, fetched with pinned SHA-256). Finding: Orekit's APM writer refuses a maneuver without MAN_DELTA_MASS (optional in the standard), so APM maneuvers are covered in the Kshana-writes direction only. Outside the case set: AEM 1.0 */RATE types and XML, repeated APM blocks</td><td><code>adm (AemMessage, ApmMessage, quaternion_a_to_b), ndm_xml</code></td></tr><tr><td>CCSDS Orbit Data Messages (OPM, OMM, OCM)</td><td>Writer and reader of the CCSDS 502.0-B-3 Orbit Data Messages in KVN and NDM/XML: OPM 3.0 and 2.0 (state vector, osculating Keplerian elements, spacecraft parameters, covariance, maneuvers, user-defined parameters), OMM 3.0 and 2.0 (mean elements by mean motion or semi-major axis, TLE-related parameters with BSTAR or BTERM and AGOM, covariance), and OCM 3.0 with trajectory (CARTP, CARTPV, CARTPVA; absolute or relative epochs), physical-properties, covariance (CARTP, CARTPV in LTM order), maneuver and user-defined blocks; a full-precision OMM from an SGP4 element set beside the unchanged OmmFile::to_omm_kvn</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>Orekit 13.1.8 (Apache-2.0) OPM, OMM and OCM parsers and writers, run as a separate program (xval/odm-orekit), pre-registered (8efea7c1) before any comparison: 27 of the 30 Kshana-written messages (6 OPM, 5 OMM and 5 OCM cases in KVN, and XML for version 3.0) parse in Orekit with every value within 1e-14 relative and every epoch within 1e-9 s (904 values, worst 0.021 of a bar), and Kshana reads all 25 messages Orekit writes 