ives reach 81 or more; all 18 pre-event ones stay at 0). RE-RUN 0.41 (D8b row 9, f09660907): R1 MET on re-run with the CUSUM restarted at each scored window's start ([monitors] roc_restart, default on): AUC 1.0000 on seen seeds 300-305 and on fresh seeds 100300-100305; R2 still at chance; the control (restart off) reproduces 0.7855. The seen-seed outcome was largely known in advance (disclosed). Internal consistency only: no real receiver or recorded interference is checked</td><td><code>iq::campaign (detect, report, runner); iq::monitor::spectral (kurtosis_reference)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Calibration of the open receiver's C/N0 and lock models to IQ campaign results, with stated prediction error</td><td>iq::labfit (campaign, cn0, iqfit, iqreport) and <code>[input] campaign</code> on <code>kshana iq labfit</code>, Python <code>kshana.iq_labfit</code> and the MCP labfit tool (campaign folders inside its work directory only): reads a <code>kshana iq campaign</code> output folder by its DIGEST and groups the scored cells into fit units (signal x loop design x front-end chain x jammer type, never pooled). Per unit, it fits measured C/N0 against stated J/S with the spectral-separation form. Q_eff is not identifiable from C/N0 data without an independent measurement of the jammer and signal powers, so Q is stated, never fitted (the type table, the event's q, or for an unknown type the most damaging stated value, cw Q = 1). The fitted parameter is the identifiable offset delta_eff = delta - 10 log10 Q, with the correlation guard reporting the degeneracy. C/N0 bins locked under 90 % are censored and listed. The threshold J/S is given directly and by the closed form; the tracking-loop and empirical lock models are coupled through the C/N0 model, with drop and re-lock dwells. A seeded cluster bootstrap over recordings (1000 replicates) gives percentile intervals; 90 % prediction intervals come from residual draws; leave-one-recording-out hold-outs are split into interpolati