bds_geo, NavParseOptions)</code></td></tr><tr><td>SP3 precise-clock interpolation</td><td>Satellite clock offset between the tabulated SP3 clock nodes by linear interpolation over the two bracketing valid nodes (the RTKLIB pephclk scheme; bad-clock sentinel skipped), and the same nodes fed to the precise-product chain as RINEX-clock-equivalent records</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>IGS final 30 s satellite clock combination (IGS0OPSFIN 30S CLK, 2025-02-24): published clock estimates at the query instants, not interpolated from the SP3; bars pre-registered in tests/fixtures/sp3_clock_igs_oracle/PREREGISTRATION.md before the first run (RMS 0.15 ns, p95 0.30 ns, node median 1e-12 s, discrimination 2x)</td><td><code>sp3 (Sp3File::clock_s, clock_nodes), precise_products (ClockRinex::from_sp3)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Carrier-phase tightly coupled GNSS/INS with float ambiguities</td><td>Error-state EKF over 15 INS states, a two-state receiver clock and one float carrier ambiguity per tracked satellite; pseudorange, carrier phase and optional range rate from an SGP4 Walker constellation (light-time and Sagnac), Klobuchar and Saastamoinen/Niell corrections applied in the loop at the filter's own position; time-differenced-carrier slip detection with a per-satellite threshold widened by the velocity uncertainty; ambiguity re-initialisation on slips and re-acquisition</td><td>MODELLED</td><td>Internal consistency: the measurements are synthesised from the models the filter uses (χ² NEES/NIS over seeds, a noise-free convergence, slip injection). MODELLED; no real receiver data or third-party filter is compared</td><td><code>fusion::carrier_tc (run_carrier_tc, CarrierTcCfg), fusion::trajectory (truth_epochs)</code></td></tr><tr><td>GNSS/INS maritime, rail and aviation packs with a tight-coupling option</td><td>Three gnss-ins scenarios on the trajectory library (a vessel weaving at 8 m/s with a five-minute outage; a train through a two-satellite cutting and a tunnel; an aircraft whose