+<td>area_trust (kshana area-trust, Python and WebAssembly): each station&#39;s epochs on a 1 s grid (Stale after 5 s with no epoch) combine into one area state with k = max(2, ceil(N/3)): UNKNOWN with fewer than 2 live stations, UNTRUSTED with at least k untrusted, DEGRADED with at least k degraded or worse or any untrusted (v2, selected by the stations document&#39;s area_rule field: at least m untrusted, m = 2 for up to 6 stations and 1 above), else TRUSTED; a worse state is published at once, a better one after 10 s. area_trust::synth builds seeded replays with injected events</td>
+<td>ReferenceImpl</td>
+<td>checked against a separate implementation in this same codebase — independent of the unit under test, but not externally authoritative — Bars pre-registered in docs/design/evidence/b5-area-trust/. T1 against an independent Python standard-library recomputation of the rule (xval/area-trust/oracle.py and oracle_v2.py); T4 on real IGS observation files (SHA-256 values in xval/area-trust/MANIFEST.tsv and MANIFEST_v2.tsv). v1: T1 MET (43 117 grid seconds of seven seeded replays, 4 to 50 stations, 520 events; the oracle&#39;s bytes); T2 MET (all 267 events with at least k stations in alarm raised the expected alert; none of the 253 with fewer raised UNTRUSTED); T3 MET (220 injected events at 100 stations, 1 Hz, over MQTT: webhook and MQTT p95 1.004 s, maximum 1.015 s; bars 5 s and 10 s); T5 MET for the files and surfaces built; T4 NOT MET: 23 alerts to DEGRADED over 13 area-days (1.77 per area-day; bar 1), none to UNTRUSTED (bar 0.1), Madrid (MADR, CEBR, YEBE, VILL), 2025-01-07 to 01-19. v2 (a two-station floor for areas of up to 6 stations, a068a3eb9): T1 MET (43 165 grid seconds, the v2 oracle&#39;s bytes), T2 MET, T3 MET (p95 1.004 s, maximum 1.013 s), T5 MET; T4 NOT MET: 16 alerts to DEGRADED or worse over 13 area-days (1.23 per area-day; bar 1), 9 of them to UNTRUSTED (0.69 per area-day; bar 0.1), Goddard (GODS, GODE, GODN, USN7), 2025-07-25 to 08-06; no alert came from one station alone, and the cause of the same-epoch alarms at several stations is not established. WHAT IS NOT CHECKED: AGC, the jamming indicator, the clock monitor and OSNMA on the real-data days (not in the files); any real interference event</td>
+<td>area_trust</td>
+<td>tests/area_trust.rs (the v1 and v2 timelines equal the oracles&#39; bytes every second; T2 alerts; boundary rules; the live rule equals the timeline; the T4 misses and T3 v2 recorded); tests/area_trust_igs.rs (T4 and T3 on the fetched IGS files, ignored by default); tests/python/test_bindings.py; web/smoke.mjs</td>
+</tr>
