+<td>locate_pd: each station&#39;s C/N0 drop (and AGC rise, where its dB-per-unit scale is stated) is turned into an interference power at the antenna; a log-distance model with the reference power profiled out, the path-loss exponent and source height marginalised and censored terms for stations that see nothing gives a posterior on a grid around the network, with its 95 % region and centroid. v2 averages each station&#39;s power over the session with one shadowing term per station, no tempering, on the stations&#39; hull buffered by 10 km; v1 is kept as recorded</td>
+<td>ReferenceImpl</td>
+<td>checked against a separate implementation in this same codebase — independent of the unit under test, but not externally authoritative — Synthetic networks drawn from a model that differs from the locator&#39;s on purpose, with an independent numpy recomputation (xval/locator-power-difference/oracle.py), under bars pre-registered in docs/design/evidence/b3a-power-difference-locator/. v1 gate (seeds 1001-2000, tau 1/60, f6b4a3336): S1 coverage MET (0.976; bar 0.90); S2 NOT MET (median 95 % region 52.5 % of the search domain; bar 25 %); S3 NOT MET (median centroid error 2.55 x the median nearest-neighbour station spacing; bar 0.5 x). v2 gate (session-level shadowing, seeds 4001-5000, 53ca11af5): NOT MET on S1 (0.890; bar 0.90; the 34 of 1 000 sessions not located count against it), S2 (26.1 %; bar 25 %) and S3 (1.45 x; bar 0.5 x); S4 determinism platforms only (Linux debug against release; the CI job b3a-v2-determinism runs it on Linux, macOS and Windows; the CLI, Python and WebAssembly half is not assessable, the locator has none of those surfaces); the numpy recomputation agrees on seeds 4001-4020 (centroids within 2.5e-10 m). By the pre-registration the real run on Jammertest 2027 is not made with this method. WHAT IS NOT CHECKED: any real interference; the C/N0 and AGC monitors themselves</td>
+<td>locate_pd</td>
+<td>tests/locator_power_difference_synthetic.rs (the v1 gate rows reproduce; the recorded v1 verdict); tests/locator_power_difference_v2.rs (12 v2 gate seeds reproduce bit for bit, debug against release; the recorded v2 verdict, the misses included; the development run seen before the gate)</td>
