ody</span><code class="lg-mod">gravity_<wbr>pds,<wbr> <wbr>body,<wbr> <wbr>propagator,<wbr> <wbr>mars_<wbr>frame</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>with_gravity_field (on Body, in src/gravity_pds.rs): attach any loaded spherical-harmonic field (for example GMM-3 or GL0660B) to a Body so the propagator evaluates it body-fixed; opt-in, default bodies unchanged</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>Internal consistency only. Each published field is defined in its producer&#x27;s body-fixed frame (GMM-3 in the Konopliv et al. 2006 Mars frame, GL0660B in the DE421 lunar principal-axis frame), while the field is evaluated in the IAU frame; the offset is not modelled</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/planetary_gravity_pds.rs::a_shadr_field_attached_to_a_body_drives_the_propagator; gravity_pds::tests::with_gravity_field_is_opt_in</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="v" data-g="orbit"><summary><span class="st st-v">Validated</span><span class="lg-req">Batch &amp; sequential orbit determination</span><code class="lg-mod">orbit_<wbr>determination,<wbr> <wbr>precise_<wbr>od <wbr>(batch_<wbr>ls::<wbr>gauss_<wbr>newton,<wbr> <wbr>fusion::<wbr>ukf)</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>Recover an epoch state [r,v] from ground-station ranges via a Gauss–Newton batch differential corrector and a sequential filter, over a two-body+J2 force model</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>Orekit 12.2 (CS GROUP, Apache-2.0) BatchLSEstimator (Levenberg–Marquardt) + KalmanEstimator (EKF) — an independent third-party estimation library on a matched force model; recovered epoch state + post-fit residual RMS agree to &lt;1e-3 m noiseless and &lt;3 m at a 5 m noise floor</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/batch_sequential_orbit_determination_reference.rs (8 scenarios: 6 noiseless LEO/MEO/eccentric/3–4-station + 2 σ=5 m, vs Orekit 12.2; worst batch |Δr| 1e-3 m / |Δv| 1e-6 m/s, sequential |Δr| 0.9 m)</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" d