by lag-1 autocorrelation</span><code class="lg-mod">allan <wbr>(lag1_<wbr>noise_<wbr>id,<wbr> <wbr>lag1_<wbr>acf)</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>allan::lag1_noise_id: the Riley and Greenhall (2004) lag-1 autocorrelation noise identifier (decimated phase with its quadratic removed, or group-averaged frequency with its line removed; repeated first differences until delta = r1/(1+r1) &lt; 0.25 or d = dmax), returning the integer and unrounded power-law exponent alpha (+2 white PM to -2 random-walk FM) at any averaging factor; it sets the noise-type degrees of freedom of the measured clock library&#x27;s device cards</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>allantools 2024.6 autocorr_noise_id (A. Wallin and contributors, LGPL-3.0-or-later, run as a separate program by the fixture generator): an independent implementation of the published Riley-Greenhall algorithm, a uniquely defined quantity under the stated conventions. Validates the identifier, not the noise content of any real clock</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/clock_library_lag1_noise_id_allantools.rs (140 cases: ten Kasdin power-law records, b = 0 to -4, as phase and frequency data, af = 1 to 64; alpha_int and d identical, worst |d alpha| 9.6e-13 and |d rho| 4.8e-13…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="v" data-g="integrity"><summary><span class="st st-v">Validated</span><span class="lg-req">Galileo OSNMA receiver-side navigation-data authentication</span><code class="lg-mod">osnma <wbr>(page,<wbr> <wbr>subframe,<wbr> <wbr>dsm,<wbr> <wbr>merkle,<wbr> <wbr>signature,<wbr> <wbr>tesla,<wbr> <wbr>mac,<wbr> <wbr>maclt,<wbr> <wbr>navdata,<wbr> <wbr>verifier,<wbr> <wbr>ubx,<wbr> <wbr>cli)</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>osnma + <code>kshana osnma verify</code>: an open, pure-Rust receiver-side verifier for Galileo OSNMA (SIS ICD Issue 1.1, Receiver Guidelines Issue 1.3) from I/NAV pages or a u-blox UBX-RXM-SFRBX stream: Merkle-tree public keys (DS